WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:02.493
- Skydiving in Dubai is spectacular,

00:00:02.493 --> 00:00:05.185
it's unlike any other place I've skydived.

00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:06.769
Once I'm in the sky,

00:00:06.769 --> 00:00:08.777
it's just like I'm like anyone else.

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:12.277
(bright electronic music)

00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:23.374
My name's Jarett Martin.

00:00:23.374 --> 00:00:24.339
I'm 26 years old.

00:00:24.339 --> 00:00:26.538
I'm from Seattle, Washington,

00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:27.959
and I'm a skydiver.

00:00:27.959 --> 00:00:30.700
My family's history is all skydiving.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.971
My grandfather was a skydiver,

00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:33.444
which led to my father being a skydiver.

00:00:33.444 --> 00:00:35.601
Then my sisters made a skydive.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.154
And my aunts and uncles are all skydivers.

00:00:38.154 --> 00:00:39.595
Of course, naturally myself.

00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:40.939
Skydiving runs in the family.

00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:44.012
Well I've been skydiving
for over 10 years now.

00:00:44.012 --> 00:00:46.467
I did my first skydive
with my father at age nine.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:50.436
And then I started on my
solo career at age 15.

00:00:50.436 --> 00:00:52.363
And I've been loving skydiving ever since.

00:00:52.363 --> 00:00:55.280
I've been disabled for eight years.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.512
I was in a weird parachuting accident

00:00:58.512 --> 00:00:59.904
when I was 18 years old.

00:00:59.904 --> 00:01:02.560
And it was a tragic accident,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.714
but I think in the end it
really made me stronger,

00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:08.927
and maybe even a better person, who knows.

00:01:08.927 --> 00:01:10.598
When I was injured,

00:01:10.598 --> 00:01:14.446
what really saved me was
the family-like attributes

00:01:14.446 --> 00:01:16.576
that skydiving has with each other.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.028
And there was no time
for me to be depressed.

00:01:19.028 --> 00:01:20.436
There was no time for me to be sad.

00:01:20.436 --> 00:01:24.292
My friends and family really
made it an easy transition

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:26.895
to what would be the
next chapter of my life.

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:30.012
I first moved to Dubai in 2013.

00:01:30.012 --> 00:01:33.764
I developed some interest
from Skydive Dubai

00:01:33.764 --> 00:01:35.029
and I got the opportunity

00:01:35.029 --> 00:01:36.954
to come out here full time.

00:01:36.954 --> 00:01:38.738
It's quite a production for me to skydive.

00:01:38.738 --> 00:01:41.384
I mean, the skydive itself of
falling out of an airplane,

00:01:41.384 --> 00:01:43.663
that's easy, but it's all of the things

00:01:43.663 --> 00:01:46.189
that lead up to getting in the airplane

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:48.065
and, you know, getting back in my wheelchair,

00:01:48.065 --> 00:01:50.049
I couldn't do it without my friends.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:52.560
And they're absolutely incredible.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.337
(atmospheric music)

00:01:56.337 --> 00:01:59.890
The views from the
height that we jump from,

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.828
you can see everything.

00:02:01.828 --> 00:02:02.661
It's one of those things,

00:02:02.661 --> 00:02:03.630
you just have to try it.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.701
It's indescribable.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:09.284
(uptempo electronic music)

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.454
There's been a couple of adaptations

00:02:19.454 --> 00:02:21.495
of equipment that I've had to use

00:02:21.495 --> 00:02:23.079
for me to be able to skydive.

00:02:23.079 --> 00:02:25.994
And one of them is my
leg retention device.

00:02:25.994 --> 00:02:28.257
It keeps my legs separated,

00:02:28.257 --> 00:02:31.835
yet it keeps them from
flapping wildly out of control.

00:02:31.835 --> 00:02:33.897
The landing is one of the most-asked

00:02:33.897 --> 00:02:35.529
questions that I get.

00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:36.914
I can't stand up my landings,

00:02:36.914 --> 00:02:38.842
like most able-bodied skydivers,

00:02:38.842 --> 00:02:42.010
so I just kind of do a glorified
tuck and roll essentially.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.027
It's as graceful of a
landing as you can get.

00:02:45.027 --> 00:02:47.806
I have probably about
close to 5,000 jumps total.

00:02:47.806 --> 00:02:50.030
And the freedom of being able

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.106
to repeat skydive after skydive

00:02:52.106 --> 00:02:53.176
while I've been in Dubai,

00:02:53.176 --> 00:02:56.926
really racked up the
jump numbers quite fast.

00:03:00.374 --> 00:03:01.289
When I'm in the zone,

00:03:01.289 --> 00:03:03.668
and I'm like really like doing my thing,

00:03:03.668 --> 00:03:05.363
it's nice to know that there's people

00:03:05.363 --> 00:03:06.538
that I'm helping,

00:03:06.538 --> 00:03:10.154
whether it be disabled people
trying to get them to do

00:03:10.154 --> 00:03:11.379
whatever they think they can do.

00:03:11.379 --> 00:03:13.061
Because if I can do skydiving,

00:03:13.061 --> 00:03:15.262
anybody can do anything.

00:03:15.262 --> 00:03:17.377
And whether it be someone disabled or not,

00:03:17.377 --> 00:03:22.074
I think it inspires
everyone to push themselves

00:03:22.074 --> 00:03:24.199
to do things that they
never thought was possible.

00:03:24.199 --> 00:03:25.051
If you think about it,

00:03:25.051 --> 00:03:26.839
like it's some guy in
a wheelchair skydiving.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.089
That doesn't seem possible.

